WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.210
Fans of the villain-slash-occasional antihero
Deathstroke are in for a treat when they catch

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.310
him in Justice League in theaters.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:11.900
Joe Manganiello, who plays Deathstroke, has
put together a pretty respectable résumé

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.920
over his roughly two decades in the film business,
but he's not quite a household name just yet.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.730
Here are a few reasons he looks so familiar.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.690
Spider-Man

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:27.250
In 2002's Spider-Man, Manganiello played infamous
bully Eugene "Flash" Thompson.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:31.760
He's horrible to Peter Parker at every opportunity,
to the point where you can't help but cheer

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.940
when he finally gets what's coming to him
in the form of Peter's first spider-powered

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:36.940
beatdown.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.560
"I like you so much I wish you had landed
that punch on Tobey Maguire."

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.159
How I Met Your Mother

00:00:44.159 --> 00:00:47.960
The years after Spider-Man were pretty lean
for Manganiello, who's been open about the

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.530
difficulties that followed his first big break.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.940
But eventually he landed a recurring role
on the hit sitcom How I Met Your Mother, joining

00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:00.850
the cast in 2006 as Brad, an old law school
friend of Jason Segel's character Marshall.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.689
Brad appeared in seven episodes, and took
on a slightly more antagonistic role in later

00:01:05.689 --> 00:01:11.340
seasons, causing drama with both Marshall
and Neil Patrick Harris' character Barney.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.549
One Tree Hill

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:19.549
Between 2008 and 2010, CW melodrama One Tree
Hill gave Manganiello his most significant

00:01:19.549 --> 00:01:21.140
TV role up to that point.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.619
He joined the show as Owen, a bar manager
who strikes up a romance with series star

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:30.649
Sophia Bush's character Brooke, and appeared
in twelve episodes over the course of three

00:01:30.649 --> 00:01:31.729
seasons.

00:01:31.729 --> 00:01:33.219
True Blood

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:37.840
Manganiello next appeared as Alcide, a hunky
werewolf who showed up in the third season

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.090
of HBO's vampire drama True Blood.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:44.979
Alcide is a fan-favorite character from the
books that inspired the show, and Manganiello

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:50.359
nailed it in 42 episodes, thanks to his natural
nice-guy charm and, well, what he looks like

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:51.450
without a shirt.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.450
"Yes.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.380
This is not news to anyone."

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.170
White Collar

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.450
Season three of the USA Network's White Collar
saw Manganiello sign on for a one-episode

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:04.869
guest appearance, which features him in an
antagonistic role as Ben, the neighbor of

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:07.829
series regular Tiffani Thiessen's character
Elizabeth.

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:12.870
It was the first time in a while Manganiello
played a full-fledged villain — experience

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:17.340
that would come in handy a few years later
when he landed the role of Deathstroke.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.780
Magic Mike

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.170
Manganiello's combination of charm and killer
physique clearly got him the right kind of

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:27.820
attention from director Steven Soderbergh,
who cast him in a memorable supporting role

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:31.090
in his 2012 smash hit dramedy Magic Mike.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.610
Manganiello appears in the film as a heartthrob
dancer with… a memorable name.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:36.730
His go-to costume?

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.300
A classic fireman getup.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:42.320
Funny enough, he almost didn't take the role
— and it was Chris Rock, of all people,

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.530
who convinced him to do it.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.440
"And I turned to Chris and I said, 'If I don't
get a shirt on soon, every guy in the world's

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.440
gonna hate my guts.'

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.480
And Chris said, 'Man, they're gonna hate your
guts anyway."

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.760
Sabotage

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:59.680
End of Watch director David Ayer cast Manganiello
in Sabotage, starring Arnold Schwarzenegger.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.590
Manganiello plays Grinder, a character mostly
recognizable due to his distinct cornrows.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:09.291
Sabotage didn't go over too well with critics
and was ultimately a box office failure, but

00:03:09.291 --> 00:03:13.900
it does feature some killer action sequences
and lots of big guys blowing stuff up — which

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.740
is kind of all you want from a movie like
this.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.730
Magic Mike XXL

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:24.600
Richie returned in the 2015 followup to Magic
Mike, coyly titled Magic Mike XXL.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.570
With the original film's Alex Pettyfer and
Matthew McConaughey not returning for the

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:32.900
sequel, Manganiello saw a significantly larger
amount of screen time in this one.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.620
Richie is also the centerpiece of what is
almost indisputably the highlight of the film,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.930
when he performs an impromptu striptease set
to "I Want it That Way" by the Backstreet

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.300
Boys right in the middle of the empty minimart.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.340
"How much for the Cheetos and water?"

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.810
Pee-wee's Big Holiday

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:53.470
Manganiello appeared in another hilarious
role soon after the Magic Mike sequel, playing

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:57.940
a fictionalized version of himself in 2016's
Pee-wee's Big Holiday.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:02.590
Unlike many cameo roles in which celebs play
themselves, Manganiello is actually a pretty

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:05.630
central character over the course of the movie.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:10.830
Manganiello plays himself as a perfect caricature—over-the-top
macho but quietly still a goofy little kid

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:11.920
at heart.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.120
"Thanks, I appreciate that."

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.120
Thanks for watching!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.290
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

